A||||2||Pontiaddict||C&D tries to roll over an Explorer||||1||
Z||000000||Pontiaddict||10-27-2000||10:50 PM||||I was reading the paper and they said that Car and Driver was testing a used Explorer in their own tire blowout test.<P>They bought a high milage Explorer at a used car lot and put a rollcage in it. The driver had a firesuit and a helmet. They put a set of new tires on it and on the back was a device that was supposed to deflate the tire in about a third of a second. They chose the back because that's where alot of the accident vehicles had bad tires and it is most likely to cause instability. They took it down Milan Dragway and had someone remotely deflate the tire at speeds between 30 and 70 mph without warning. The driver hit the brakes without turning the wheel and stopped the Explorer without problems.<P>Of course.... <P>The Firestones didn't blow out, they blew the tread off of the tire and ususlly had air in them after the accident. Most people pull off the road when the tire goes, and that usually involves turning the wheel. Most roads have turns and rough pavement unlike a drag strip. So the test wasn't really accurate. If they would find a blown out tire, put it on the car and do some handling tests on it, I might think that the test had some merit.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-28-2000||02:34 PM||||A blow out test completly fails to duplicate the primary problem of tread sep. namely the fact the tread can wrap up the axle and jam the wheel. This happens very sudenly and with no warning. It's a whole diferant condition than a blowout. Such a jam can and likely will jerk a vehicle sideways real quick. On a front wheel it's almost certain to tear the steering wheel from the drivers hands no matter what kind of grip is being used.<P>What issue is that in?||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||10-28-2000||03:10 PM||||It's gotta sound like holy hell when a tire tread separates...that has to result in a panic among drivers that causes a lot of what has happened to drivers in these instances.<P>Compound that with a vehicle with screaming kids/back seat passengers and it's no wonder so many of them roll over.||||reg||1
